Browser evaluation of the page served by `soft-foundry ui --port 4877` from this repository
(21 records: 3 open, 18 closed). Chrome on macOS, dark colour scheme, driven through the Claude in
Chrome extension; values are what the live DOM and screenshots showed. The page's three files are
byte-identical at 93b9422 (when most of this was observed) and 5d36e6f (the verified commit); the
final pass (board, landmarks, tab order, focus ring, pause) was at 5d36e6f.

EVAL-004 the board
  title "Changes · Soft Foundry"; h1 "Changes"; lede "3 open changes, none failing. 18 closed records."
  Open (3): ui-server sixteen pending/optional cells; ui-snapshot pass at 00, 05, 06, 07, 13, 15 and waived
    or optional elsewhere, flag "3 advisories"; upstream-failure-reporting pass at 00.
  Closed (18): recorded-complete marks (ring with a dot), distinct from evaluated pass (filled disc).
  Column numbers 00..15 share one baseline (one distinct top offset across sixteen headers).
  No console errors.

EVAL-005 one change, its gates, and staying current
  #/change/ui-snapshot: h1 is the title; meta line slug, status, risk, type, branch; "Gated track."
    Sixteen gates in order; 15 learn selected by default (last completed); panel lists nine checks.
  #/change/cross-cli-hooks (closed): note "This record is closed. Its stale gates mean code has changed
    since its evidence was recorded, which is expected once a change has merged." 06 verify selected by
    default (first stale); its failing check is "evidence current" with the changed paths.
  Clicking 13 review: hash becomes #/change/cross-cli-hooks/review, that button alone has
    aria-expanded="true", panel heading "13 review: Stale", focus stays on the button.
  Live update: with #/change/ui-server open and focus on the intake gate, the handoff was edited from
    in_progress back to pending on disk. Within one poll the gate read "Pending", focus was still on
    the intake gate, and the live region read "This change was updated at 23:55:35."
  Hidden tab: while document.hidden was true the "Updated" time did not advance (no polling).
  Pause: aria-pressed true and "Paused"; pressing again resumes.
  First navigation from an extension-driven tab was answered 403 "the request came from another site"
    at 0d69a4d's design; fixed before GREEN (see 05-implementation/deviations.md).

EVAL-006 accessibility
  Keyboard: tab order is skip link, wordmark, Changes, Pause updates, the Open table's scroll region,
    each change link, the Closed table's scroll region, and so on. Gates are buttons. A real Tab press
    put a 3px solid outline (rgb 127,176,240) on the focused link; :focus-visible matched.
  Structure: html lang="en"; header, nav, main, footer; one h1 per view; h2 per section; tables have a
    caption, th scope="col" and scope="row"; each cell carries its state as a visually hidden word.
  Colour: each state has its own shape and a word. Text contrast, computed from the palette:
    light  ink 13.8, steel 5.4, pour 5.1, sound 5.4, flaw 5.5, cold 5.8 on the ground (4.5 needed)
    dark   ink 14.8, steel 7.9, pour 7.2, sound 8.5, flaw 7.9, cold 8.0 on the ground
  Reflow: with the body constrained to 320 CSS px, nothing outside the two table scroll regions
    extended past 320 px on either view; gates wrapped two to a row at 120 px each.
  Target size: gate buttons 120 by 101; Pause 32 high; standalone links were 18 high and were given
    block padding to reach 24.
  Motion: one animation (the in-progress gate's top edge), off under prefers-reduced-motion.

Not exercised, and said so in results.md: a screen reader; the light scheme on screen (contrast is
computed, not viewed); 200% browser zoom; a real 320 px viewport (the window would not go below 500).
